.col-6 .col-md-4

The combination of .col-6 and .col-md-4 in Bootstrap creates a responsive element that changes its width based on the screen size. 
Here is how the element will behave across different screen breakpoints:

Screen Size 
	Breakpoint	Screen Width	Columns Occupied			Width 									Percentage
	Extra 		Small				None (.col-6 applies)	Less than 576px	6 (out of 12)	50%
	Small			sm	≥ 576px		6 (out of 12)															50%
	Medium		md	≥ 768px		4 (out of 12)															33.3%
	Large			lg	≥ 992px		4 (out of 12)															33.3%
	Extra 		Large	xl	≥ 1200px	4 (out of 12)														33.3%
Explanation

    .col-6: This is a base class that applies to all screen sizes (extra small and up) because it has no specific breakpoint infix. It makes the element take up 6 columns (50% width).
    .col-md-4: This class applies when the screen width is at the "medium" breakpoint (768px) or larger. When this condition is met, this class's styles override the .col-6 class for that specific breakpoint and all larger ones. 

In essence: The element will be 50% wide on mobile devices and small tablets, and automatically become 33.3% wide on medium-sized screens (like larger tablets and laptops) and any larger screen sizes. 